WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.999
I don't know how many times I had heard or at least observed some form of the idea. That classic overused cliché:

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:12.179
that one's whole life flashes before their eyes in the conscious moments right before dying. I had heard it a lot –

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:15.719
I know that. I had even heard it used in plenty of non death related

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.400
instances, when people just wanted to add a little grandiose to a situation or story. I

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:26.670
myself had probably even used it in a story or two. It is, of course, one of those things that doesn't really make much sense

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:31.019
while you're alive, though. After all, how could one's entire life flash before their eyes?

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.790
Presumably, the use of the word "eyes" here is meant to represent sort of the "visualization"

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.479
center of the mind, as opposed to literally the eyeballs in the head.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:45.689
But even still, how could the mind speed up years worth of experiences so fast that it could all be perceived and

00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:49.199
recollected in minutes, or even seconds, and still be discernible?

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.249
I had always wondered at the absurdity of the notion whenever it was mentioned or

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:58.469
represented in something. Now, in this moment, on the side of the road, contorted and lacerated,

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:00.869
I was about to find out exactly what it meant.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.710
I didn't know exactly how much blood the human body could lose before dying,

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.679
but it didn't take long for me to realize that I was getting pretty close.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:14.699
I could feel my body shutting down and started experiencing weird pains that didn't hurt so much as confused and nauseated me.

00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:20.639
Harder to describe than it was to feel. I could also hear that people were saying things to me that were indicative of someone dying:

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:24.419
things like, "Please don't close your eyes. Just hold on a little bit longer.

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:28.499
It's going to be okay. An ambulance is on the way." Stuff like that,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.529
but with different words and in a much more pleading, dramatic tone.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:37.049
They all knew as well as I did, though, what was happening, and that no amount of force of will to keep my eyes open

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:40.589
was going to outmatch death if it were to come. At this point

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.159
It felt much better to just close my eyes

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:48.029
anyway. It somehow relieved the pain a little. I accepted that I was dying by this point wasn't even really a conscious choice

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:52.079
My body knew my mind knew after this moment of acceptance

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:58.409
my mind certainly did race at a sort of flash like speed but mostly it felt comparable to that of what I would imagine a

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.290
Lucid panic attack feels like on 20 cups of coffee

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:08.339
I didn't see everything from my life and there was no apparent rhyme or reason or order of which I did I did however feel

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.450
a great sense of regret

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:09.819
as I

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:13.229
ruminated across all the feelings and thoughts and memories that appeared I

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.589
I thought about who I would never see again and what I would never do again

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:20.460
I thought about how I wouldn't see what colors were going to be in the next evening sunset

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.420
How I would never brush my teeth again

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.580
How I would never feel the air running over my skin or flowing into my nose again

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.809
I thought about the low hum of all the appliances in my house that I would never hear again

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.100
Then I thought about what I never saw or did but always wanted to all the times

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.089
I never told people how I felt or how much I cared about them all the opportunities

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:44.550
I let go because I was scared all the habits and problems in my life that I always wanted to change but never did

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:51.209
Then I thought about how much time I wasted worrying about these things the time I wasted hating myself the time I wasted being

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:56.100
Unhappy in the time I wasted getting mad at myself for being unhappy when I should have been happy

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:01.649
I thought about how I rarely ever fully synced up with what I knew I should have done or how I should have thought

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.889
How I seem to always deceive or sabotage myself in the process

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.899
I would get close to the sort of ideal or sublime that I always knew existed in each moment

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:15.330
But then I would run the other way. However, upsetting and sad this whole part was, it kind of fit my Hollywood

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.480
expectations of dying which only added to the disappointment

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.899
It was anticlimactic like predicting the end of a movie

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:28.860
Now I found myself getting upset and angry about the disappointingly rational and predictable process of getting upset

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.010
angry and regretful while dying even here

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.929
I was literally regretting my final moments of life as they occurred "how foolish could I be?"

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:43.859
I wondered what kind of being hates itself or brings suffering onto itself knowing that hating itself and suffering makes them miserable

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:50.549
What kind of being spends their final moments alive being miserable about their life? In this ridiculous self-loathing

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:57.839
Rumination as if coerced by something that was predetermined to happen at a certain moment of the body and brain turning off a sudden pause

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.310
Occurred a pause that felt much more like a flash than the previous flash that was occurring

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:08.279
It was not a flash of speed but a sudden flash of ceasing speed like a camera flash to a little rodent

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.470
it stunned me and stopped everything as

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:17.730
If my consciousness had finally surrendered told by my subconscious that there was no self or life left to defend for the first time

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.149
I felt free not free in the sense that I was able to do

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:25.080
Whatever. I wanted quite the opposite free in the sense that in only a few moments

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:33.050
I literally would not be able to do anything I wanted. In this I suddenly became so majorly indifferent to everything that everything became clear

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.720
I saw myself through an entirely different lens as if a smudge on my pre-existing lens had been cleared off

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.089
Revealing what had always been obstructed from me

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:45.770
I continued thinking for a little while but my thinking was different there wasn't critical

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.839
Rational or judgmental for the first time in my entire life. I saw who I really was

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:55.189
While alive I understood that I had a conscious brain and unconscious brain

00:04:55.190 --> 00:05:02.330
I had learned about these fairly rudimentary psychology concepts as a young child and considered the implications of them frequently throughout my life

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:07.939
However, these terms never really translated in any practical or helpful way at least not for me

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:13.159
If anything they only made me feel like I had two parts of my brain the part that was me and the part

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:20.179
That wasn't. I was of course my conscious brain and my unconscious brain was something else that I was constantly fighting or trying to conquer

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:26.179
This wasn't wrong per say, but it wasn't exactly right either at a minimum, It certainly wasn't helpful

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:32.960
It took being mangled on the side of a road with parts of my brain seemingly being turned off to actually understand it. Sure

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:34.770
I was never my unconscious brain

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:40.609
But I was never my conscious brain either just like I was never my heart or my hand or anything else on its own

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:45.770
I was never even solely what was contained inside my body. I was everything in and out

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:50.419
I was the puppet and the puppeteer the puppeteer being sort of my unconscious brain

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:55.490
But also way more than my unconscious brain it was what made and fueled my unconscious brain

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.700
What made my brain as a whole. What made everything.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:06.650
Admittedly while alive this might have sounded confusing or pretentiously cheesy or like spiritual nonsense or even cliche if someone had told me

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.810
Perhaps it is to you right now

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:14.390
Most things about life while I was alive though sounded confusing pretentiously cheesy or like spiritual nonsense

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:18.380
However, after a certain point of being viscerally aware of your approaching mortality

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.450
You sort of don't think about things like that anymore

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:26.779
You stopped putting this filter of judgment on top of sincerity or cliche archetypal experiences regardless

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:32.090
Even if you're not in this state if you can humor me just for a moment, imagine the puppet and puppeteer. I referred to

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:37.400
Consider how a puppeteer is only a puppeteer if it has and manipulates a puppet

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:42.299
If there was no such thing as a puppet, there would be no such thing as a puppeteer and vice versa

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:46.020
The puppet is not the puppeteer and the puppeteer is not the puppet

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:50.579
But without the other both ceased to exist in the context of their definitions

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:56.760
I spent my whole life thinking I was the puppet contained by the strings the consciousness contained by the brain the brain

00:06:56.890 --> 00:07:01.049
Contained by the body the body contained by the world and as a result

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:03.390
I spent my whole life at war against everything

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.179
I felt contained by I spent my life pulling at the strings

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:10.259
Trying to rip myself from them these strings and my pulling at them

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:10.600
however

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:17.309
Was the source of all the self sabotage and self-loathing all the divisions and limits between what I wanted for myself and what I never

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:20.579
Could have I was contained by strings and furthermore

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:26.700
I added constant tension to them by pulling at them making things worse by always trying to make things better.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:32.339
A little earlier I would have been gravely regretful of this realization far more than my earlier regrets

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:38.549
I would have tormented over the idea that I ruined my life missing the entire point making things worse than they had to be

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:39.330
however

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:45.630
I did not get mad or regretful at all by this point my conscious sense of self had fully given up on defending itself

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:52.109
I didn't care. I recognized that I had no choice in these strings existing in the first place. They were written in my DNA

00:07:52.479 --> 00:07:55.529
They were written in the DNA of my DNA and furthermore

00:07:55.530 --> 00:08:00.089
I had no choice in pulling at them either if I was both the puppet and the puppeteer

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:05.640
Even the act of pulling on these strings and struggling towards something was in fact part of the whole show

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:09.930
My being came with strings and my being came with the desire to pull at the strings

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.589
So what was I to do other than to live with strings and pull at them?

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:20.070
I spent my whole life fighting Who I was often hating who I was trying to be happier or better or something

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:26.760
Sometimes I would be successful but even then would mostly just return to the same starting point beginning the fight all over again

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.149
But of course this was because I never was who I thought I was

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:34.200
This part of myself that I always thought I was in a fight with turns out

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:39.030
It was actually more of a dance and without the constant push and pull without the struggle

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:44.729
Without seemingly having missed the point there would have been no point at all. No dance. No show.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.630
The things I could have changed

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:53.079
I did the things I couldn't I didn't and the things I didn't know I should have I never thought to try. I was exactly

00:08:53.079 --> 00:08:58.299
Who I could have been exactly who I needed to be. I did everything right by doing a great deal of things wrong

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:03.639
There was nothing to regret regret implies that I chose how things went, but I never really had a choice at all

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:09.789
I didn't choose who I was anymore or any less than anything else that is was or ever will be no more than a dog

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.519
Chooses to be a dog or rock chooses to be a rock

00:09:12.519 --> 00:09:15.758
I just woke up and was I didn't choose who my parents were

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.729
Who my brain was like when my body was like well

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:25.630
my first sight was my first conscious experience my anxieties my fears or any of what these things caused me to do. Now, I was

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.759
about to fall asleep forever in the last choice

00:09:27.759 --> 00:09:28.880
I never made

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:34.809
Holding the thing that I had been chasing my whole life what had been the source of my misery was now in the final moment

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:42.250
The source of my bliss the source of my self-discovery my acceptance of who I really was while alive and Who I am now

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.620
while dead

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.490
 

